{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapKeystone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapKeystone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassGap","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.substrateGap_of_crossingFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.substrateGap_of_crossingFiltration","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L233-L260","doc":"**S1c-(iii) reduction.** In the substrate window `1 < q ≤ 2`\n(which contains the physical `q₀ ≈ 1.11`), the crossing-energy\nfiltration implies the uniform substrate gap: there\n`(q − 1)² ≤ 1`, so `Δ_q = E_×(q)·(q−1)² ≤ E_×(q)`, and any\neigenvalue dominating one crossing's energy dominates the gap\nbound.\n\nThis reduces S1c to establishing `CrossingFiltration` for the\nconcrete tower — a single named hypothesis replacing the informal\n\"min-energy-per-crossing\" argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingFiltration.per_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingFiltration.per_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L230-L230","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingFiltration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingFiltration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L229-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingFiltration","kind":"class","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L219-L231","doc":"**Crossing-energy filtration** (S1c strategy (iii) as a named\nhypothesis): every non-vacuum eigenvalue of every tower level\ncarries at least one crossing's worth of energy `E_×(q)`.\n\nThis is the \"min-energy-per-crossing counting\" mechanism of the\nworkplan — every non-trivial excitation contains ≥ 1 crossing and\ncrossings contribute additively ≥ `minCrossingEnergy q`.\nEstablishing this for the concrete brane tower is the\nresearch-grade content of S1c; here it is the named interface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.substrateGap_of_uniform_gapValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.substrateGap_of_uniform_gapValue","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L192-L217","doc":"**S1b bridge theorem.** If every level of a brane-tower family of\ntransfer matrices has its first excited eigenvalue (`gapValue`)\nbounded below by `massGapBound q` — i.e. the per-level\n`YangMillsMassGap.mass_gap` inequality holds uniformly — then the\nuniform-in-`n` substrate gap holds on the tower spectrum.\n\nThe proof uses exactly the spectral interface of\n`def:categorical-transfer-matrix`: the vacuum eigenvalue is `0`\n(`vacuum_eigenvalue`) and eigenvalues are monotone\n(`eigenvalues_mono`), so every non-vacuum eigenvalue dominates\n`gapValue = eigenvalues 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap.gap_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap.gap_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L190-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap.one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap.one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L189-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L188-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateGap","kind":"class","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L180-L190","doc":"Uniform-in-`n` substrate gap, conditional form (§3b-cond\nconditional-class pattern), parametrized by the level-`n`\nexcitation spectrum.  Downstream consumers take this class as an\nexplicit `[Instance]` hypothesis per the conditional-class\ndiscipline; `substrateGap_of_uniform_gapValue` and\n`substrateGap_of_crossingFiltration` below provide the two\ninstantiation routes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.towerSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.towerSpectrum","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L171-L178","doc":"The level-indexed excitation spectrum of a brane-tower family of\ncategorical transfer matrices: at level `n`, the set of\neigenvalues of `tms n`.  This pins the `spectrum` parameter of\n`SubstrateGap` to the corpus-canonical spectral interface\n`QOU.Torsion.CategoricalTransferMatrix`\n(`def:categorical-transfer-matrix`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_one_add_eps_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_one_add_eps_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L136-L167","doc":"**Two-sided ε³ pinch**: for every `0 < ε`,\n\n`ε³/2 ≤ Δ_{1+ε} ≤ ε³`.\n\n(The lower bound uses `1 + ε ≤ 2 + ε`; the upper uses\n`2 + ε ≤ 2(1 + ε)`, i.e. `0 ≤ ε` — neither needs `ε ≤ 1`.)\nThis is the quantitative content of `Δ_q = ε³(1 + O(ε))` and makes\nthe standard-part-zero claim of the workplan immediate: the gap is\nsqueezed between two infinitesimals of order exactly 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_one_add_eps_div_hbarSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_one_add_eps_div_hbarSq","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L117-L134","doc":"**ε³ lemma, physical-units form (exact cubic).** At `q = 1 + ε`,\nwith `ℏ_q = (q−1)/q = ε/(1+ε)`:\n\n`Δ_{1+ε} / ℏ_{1+ε}² = ε + (3/2)·ε² + (1/2)·ε³`.\n\nThis is an exact polynomial — the workplan's\n`Δ_q/ℏ_q² = ε + 3⁄2·ε² + O(ε³)` with the `O(ε³)` term pinned to\nexactly `ε³/2`.  The physical-units gap dies *linearly* in `ε`;\nits standard part at the classical point is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_one_add_eps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_one_add_eps","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L103-L115","doc":"**ε³ lemma, categorical form (exact).** At `q = 1 + ε`:\n\n`Δ_{1+ε} = ε³ · (2 + ε) / (2(1 + ε))`.\n\nThe factor `(2+ε)/(2(1+ε))` tends to `1` as `ε → 0`, so this is\nthe exact form of the workplan target `Δ_q = ε³(1 + O(ε))`; the\nquantitative pinch is `massGapBound_one_add_eps_bounds` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_div_hbarSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.massGapBound_div_hbarSq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapKeystone.lean#L85-L99","doc":"**Exact physical-units identity**\n`Δ_q / ℏ_q² = ½·q·(q−1)·(q+1)` with `ℏ_q = (q−1)/q`.\nProbe-verified at 50 dps by `q1_mass_gap_probe.py`\n(`q1-mass-gap-probe.witness.json`, field `exact_identities`).\n\nPositivity (`massGapBound_pos`), vanishing at the classical point\n(`massGapBound_at_one`), and monotonicity (`massGapBound_mono`)\nlive upstream in `QOU.Torsion.MassGap`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}